WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.440
You know, it's funny, sometimes American journalists
talk about how bad a country is

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.020
because: ‘People are lining up for food.’

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.600
That's a good thing.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.560
In other countries, people don't line up for
food.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.140
The rich get the food and the poor starve
to death.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.220
The distribution of wealth in this country

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.480
is one of the most unfair and distorted in
the entire world

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.640
I think you change it through tax law,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.220
I think you change it through public ownership
of significant parts of the economy.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.740
Everybody was totally convinced that Castro
was the worst guy in the world.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.500
They forgot that he educated their kids, gave
them healthcare,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.960
totally transformed their society.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.040
Throughout his career,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.740
Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders has explained
away the inevitable downsides

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.140
of massively increasing the power of the state
over the individual.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.460
It's a dictatorship.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.110
It's a poor economy.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.240
We want changes.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.740
But have some good things been done in Cuba?

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.600
Yes.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.180
Sanders once identified as a “radical socialist”

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.460
who admired the achievements of Cuba under
Fidel,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.460
of Nicaragua under the Sandinistas,

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.500
and of the Soviet Union right up to the fall
of the Berlin Wall.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.240
Their public transportation system was the
cleanest,

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.379
most effective mass transit system that I've
ever seen in my life.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:07.220
The stations themselves were absolutely beautiful,
uh,

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.380
including many works of art, chandeliers that
were beautiful.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.660
Running for office in the 70s,

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.260
Sanders sought a top tax rate of 100%.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.880
Saying nobody should earn more than a million
dollars.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.600
Sanders wanted to stop businesses from moving
out of their original communities.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.120
Saying the ultimate solution to protect workers
was national legislation

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.630
that would “bring about the public ownership
of the major means of production"

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.380
He favored “the public ownership of utilities,
banks, and major industries,”

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.120
without compensation to investors and stockholders.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.420
Face it, you don't find many socialists in
elective office in this country.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.140
And one is elected mayor of a sizeable city
well that's news.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.840
Shortly after he was elected mayor of Burlington,
Vermont, in 1981,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.660
Sanders told a room full of charity workers,
“I don’t believe in charities,”

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.680
because only the government should provide
social services to the needy.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.700
Do I believe that the profit motive is fundamental
to human nature?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.340
The answer is no.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.979
I think the spirit of cooperation, that you
and I can work together better

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.720
rather than have to compete against each other
and try to destroy each other.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.240
Healthcare is a right-

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.140
Today he calls himself a “Democratic Socialist,”

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.880
and has himself become a millionaire.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.620
I wrote a best selling book, you write a best
selling book you can be a millionaire too.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.300
He favors single-payer health care, free public
college for all, and a $15 minimum wage.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.040
We're not talking about Venezuela, we're not
talking about Cuba.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.220
So the next time that you hear me attacked
as a socialist, remember this:

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:33.240
I don't believe government should take over,
you know, the grocery store down the street,

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.460
or own the means of production.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.219
But one thing has remained constant

00:02:37.219 --> 00:02:41.819
as Sanders has shifted his model for U.S.
policy from Nicaragua, Cuba, and the USSR

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:43.750
to Denmark, Finland, and Sweden:

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:47.340
In all of these countries, he’s misled his
followers about what’s really happening.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.680
As a socialist the word socialism does not
frighten me

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.129
and I think it's probably fair to say that
the Nicaraguan government

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.010
is primarily a socialist government.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.400
The government there has the strange and unusual
idea

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.389
that they should attempt to do something for
the people of Nicaragua

00:03:04.389 --> 00:03:07.560
rather than for the United States corporations.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.739
They are now teaching poetry, not only to
peasants and to workers

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.740
but in the military, in the police department.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.180
When Sanders was the mayor of Burlington Vermont

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.500
he vowed that he would defy the Reagan administration's embargo

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.520
against Nicaragua and the Sandinistas

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.779
who had overthrown an American-backed dictator

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.740
and instituted a revolutionary socialist government.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.000
In 1985, Sanders traveled to Nicaragua

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.500
to attend a celebration in honor of the revolution’s
sixth anniversary.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.340
I mean, it's unbelievable to say that a mayor
of a city of 38,000

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:41.740
is now the highest ranking American to visit
them during the celebration of their revolution.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.120
I was treated in a special way.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.880
Surrounded by reporters at the airport upon
his return,

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.980
Sanders was enthusiastic about what he had
seen in Nicaragua.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.940
Many of the things that we saw were impressive,

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.840
there's a tremendous sense of energy.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.380
Sanders praised the Sandinista leadership
and president Daniel Ortega.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.380
Ortega is an impressive guy,

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.780
Erensto Cardenal is a funny looking guy, he has gray hair,

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.380
and he really does remind you of the hippie.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.840
They are not, to quote Ronald Reagan loony
toon characters

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.340
I just went all around, stop people and ask
them 'are you with the government or not?'

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.040
They kinda laugh, they don't quite understand
what you're talking about.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.400
Of course they're with the government.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.900
Now obviously I will be attacked by every
editorial writer in the free press

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.360
for being a dumb dupe.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.800
Maybe I am.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.520
I was impressed by their intelligence and
by their sincerity

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.270
these are not political hacks.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.820
He praised the seizure of private farms and
businesses.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:32.460
In terms of land reform, giving for the first
time in their lives,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.840
real land to farmers.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.050
The people of Nicaragua, the poor people,
respect that.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.340
Rich people, needless to say who used to have
the good life there

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.980
are not terribly happy.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.780
What Sanders didn't mention was that by 1985

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.240
international watchdog groups

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.860
had exposed the Sandinistas significant human
rights violations.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.100
A 1981 report by the inter American commission
on human rights

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.900
revealed mass executions and persecution of
indigenous peoples.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.159
And just two years before Sanders made his
trip

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.520
Time Magazine reported that hundreds of citizens

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.780
were disappearing every month at the hands
of the Sandinistas.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.320
Many of us get depressed about what's going
on in Nicaragua today

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.000
and the absolute lies that are coming out
of the White House.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.480
In fact we have a right to be very exhilarated.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.840
Sanders accused the American government and
media

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.919
of conspiring to cover up a Socialist success story.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.700
The important story is not Nicaragua.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.700
When you read the New York Times, the real
truth is not being told

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.520
and how that's obfuscated, ok, that's what's
the interesting story.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.830
And if you get on the air and you say, 'I
am sympathetic to the Sandinista government

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.569
I think it was right they made their revolution

00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:31.540
they're trying to do the right thing, no good.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.460
My point to Ortega is they are not getting
their message

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.260
of what they are trying to do out to the American
people.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.599
It's, I just came back from a 14 hour trip
so I-

00:05:47.599 --> 00:05:51.660
The Sandinistas would remain in power for
five more years after Sander's visit

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.860
and the Nicaraguan permanent commission on
human rights

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.990
would go on to document over 14,000 instances
of rape, torture and murder during their reign.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.690
They really were talking about a transformation
of society,

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.539
giving power to the poor people, to the working
people

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:07.401
and that has caused the conflict, needless
to say in Nicaragua

00:06:07.401 --> 00:06:09.060
which we're seeing today.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.480
I remember for some reason or another

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.880
being very excited when Fidel Castro made the revolution in Cuba,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.659
I was a kid and I remember reading that.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:23.400
It just seemed right and appropriate that
poor people were rising up against

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.000
rather ugly rich people.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.920
While Sanders was still mayor of Burlington

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.629
he traveled to Cuba in 1989 to seek a meeting
with Fidel Castro

00:06:30.629 --> 00:06:33.380
though he ended up settling for the mayor
of Havana.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.820
By this time, Castro had seized private farms
and businesses,

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.770
imprisoned artists, created informant squads
to monitor and arrest dissenters

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:44.180
and forced gay citizens and other undesirables
into labor camps.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:47.580
Everybody was totally convinced that Castro
was the worst guy in the world,

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:51.340
that all the cuban people were going to rise
up in rebellion against Fidel Castro.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.090
They forgot that he educated their kids, gave
them healthcare,

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.000
totally transformed the society, you know,

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.569
not to say that Fidel Castro or Cuba are perfect,
they are certainly not.

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:04.240
Castro was open about his need to eliminate
individual rights in order to ensure collective rights.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.939
He understood that curbing press freedoms

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.980
was a prerequisite for the success of a socialist
government.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.500
Saying he couldn't tolerate dissidence in
the mass media

00:07:11.509 --> 00:07:13.909
because the people's cohesion is fundamental.

00:07:13.909 --> 00:07:17.500
If you asked us if a paper could appear here
against socialism

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.550
I could say honestly no it can not appear
here

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:27.520
in that sense we do not have the freedom of
the press that you possess in the US.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.529
But Sanders disagreed with Castro,

00:07:29.529 --> 00:07:32.310
he thought the American press was similarly
compromised

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.219
because it was controlled by politicians and
big money interests.

00:07:35.219 --> 00:07:36.840
Beginning to read about the Cuban revolution

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.220
and thought what I was more impressed about

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.820
is how it was being reported in the United
States Press

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.680
I mean I began to understand that you don't
always hear all of the truth.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:47.780
For example just last night I was watching
Canadian television which we get down here,

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.240
it was a program on Cuba,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.580
we're not allowed to see those programs here
in the United States.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.060
Just because Ronald Reagan dislikes these
people

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:58.320
does not mean to say that the people in their
own nations feel the same way.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.760
Today the Cuban government censors the internet,

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.880
bans public displays of affection between
gay couples,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.440
and jails people for criticizing the government.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:09.719
You could say there's some positive things
in Cuba, there's some very negative things.

00:08:09.719 --> 00:08:13.720
50 years after the revolution people still
can't dissent with freedom,

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:14.720
the economy is terrible.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.660
But, you know, it's somehow

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.440
they've decided that Cuba is the only non-democratic country in the world.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:28.680
Glory to the great soviet people, the builders
of communism.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.440
The problem with the world socialism is that
very often it's been equated

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.840
with what happens in the Soviet Union

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.180
with it's authoritarianism and totalitarianism.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.660
I believe very strongly in the right of dissent.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:42.340
Sanders traveled to the Soviet Union in 1988,
three years before its collapse.

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:45.310
He'd gotten married to his second wife Jane
the day before leaving

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:47.160
and the trip doubled as what he called, quote:

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.640
"A very strange honeymoon."

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:54.620
Sanders formalized its relationship with its
Russian sister city Yaroslavl

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:57.860
and praised the communist government's social
and cultural achievements.

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:01.740
We went to a theater in Yaroslavl which was
absolutely beautiful,

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.720
had three separate stages including a puppeteer
area

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.920
and of course the highest price of the ticket
that you could get

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.840
was the equivalent of a dollar fifty.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.840
En route home, a journalist confronted him
again at the airport

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.060
with reporting by the Associated Press of
dilapidated, unsanitary living conditions

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.140
and food shortages in Yaroslavl.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.820
There was no hot water and no food?

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:22.440
Yeah.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:26.720
You know I can't, none of us did an exhaust-

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.820
an exhaustive study of living conditions
in Yaroslavl.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:34.140
I didn't notice much deprivation, how it is
that a fair statement?

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.140
Later he said he was impressed by Soviet official's
transparency

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:39.149
in acknowledging their housing crisis.

00:09:39.149 --> 00:09:41.080
Which he found comparable to America's.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.120
There's a major housing crisis which they
acknowledge.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.740
But the acknowledge that not only do they
not have enough housing,

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:52.260
the the construction and the quality of that
housing is also not adequate,

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.560
and they were very free to mention that.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.560
But you know one had isolated situations say
look, socialism has failed over there,

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.760
compared to what?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.420
You know that in the United States of America
today

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.780
the average married couple can no longer afford
a home.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:08.040
Sanders also appreciated the Soviets openness
about other issues

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.220
and believed policymakers in the US had much
to learn from the Communist system.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:17.620
They are absolutely open in acknowledging
that they are not a democratic society.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:19.360
Their healthcare system is free

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.400
but they would be open to acknowledge that
it is probably ten years

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.680
behind the United States in terms of medical
technology.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.720
We were willing to be critical of the United
States,

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.700
we were there to say 'yeah, we have problems,
you have problems.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:34.500
there are strengths to the US system, there
are strengths to our system.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.880
our goal is to take the strengths of both
systems.'

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:42.680
This land was made for you and me!

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.720
What I believe in has nothing to do with communism.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:58.029
After a failed run for governor of Vermont
in 1986,

00:10:58.029 --> 00:10:59.580
around the fall of the Soviet Union,

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.519
Sanders set his sights on higher office.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.060
You know we freed the slaves a long long time
ago.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:08.000
But in many respects the average working person
today has very little rights.

00:11:08.009 --> 00:11:10.350
He re-branded himself a democratic socialist

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.640
and won a seat in Congress in 1990.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:17.240
Authoritarian communism has been a vicious
political system

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:22.160
which, over its length of time, has resulted
in the murder of many many millions of people.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:26.420
As an economic system it has not succeeded
and I'm delighted to see its demise.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:29.220
That has nothing to do with democratic socialism.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.260
Toiday Sanders objects to comparisons between
his policies

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.420
and those of the Sandinistas or Castros.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.860
When I talk about democratic socialism,

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.220
I'm not looking at Venezuela, I'm not looking
at Cuba,

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.200
I'm looking at countries like Denmark and
Sweden.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.960
What hasn't changed is Sanders' unwillingness
to acknowledge

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:50.220
the political and economic realities of the
countries he points to as models.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:53.310
Scandinavia is a bastion of free market capitalism.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:57.080
In the libertarian Frasier Institute's 2018
Human Freedom Index,

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:00.449
Norway, Denmark and Finland ranked higher
than the United States

00:12:00.449 --> 00:12:05.120
and in 2015 the Danish prime minister directly
contradicted Sanders' claims.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:10.880
I know that some people in the US associate
the nordic model with some sort of socialism.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.400
Therefore I would like to make one thing clear.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:18.520
Denmark is far from a socialist planned economy.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:22.420
It might surprise some of you but Forbes named
Denmark

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.640
the best country in the world for business.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.080
Denmark does offer expansive social benefits,

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:31.340
including single payer healthcare, free education,
and months of payed family leave.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.240
What is the catch you would ask

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:36.399
and of course the high taxes.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.440
The top income tax in Denmark is almost 60%.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.280
When you think about 90% you don't think that's
obviously too high?

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.020
No.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:52.459
Danish citizens also pay a 25% sales tax and
excise taxes on cars of up to 180%.

00:12:52.459 --> 00:12:56.180
But tax revenue in nordic countries isn't
enough to pay for their social programs

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.380
which are unsustainable in their current form.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:03.540
We have no choice but to reform our society
in order to preserve the welfare state

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.480
and the public support for it.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:10.080
Sweden is raising its retirement age and further
privatizing parts of its healthcare system.

00:13:10.089 --> 00:13:12.529
In Finland the coalition government recently
resigned

00:13:12.529 --> 00:13:16.740
after it failed to pass reforms it viewed
as crucial to averting financial ruin.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:21.509
Denmark is increasing its retirement age to
73 and cutting spending and taxes.

00:13:21.509 --> 00:13:24.779
The answer can not always be spend more money.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:29.420
I want to improve our competitiveness, reduce
taxes for business,

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.480
remove red tape.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.920
Sanders also points to Norway as a model,

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:37.200
a country where massive oil production subsidizes
the welfare benefits

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:41.300
of a population that's roughly 62 times smaller
than in the US.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:45.040
He never acknowledges fundamental differences
between the nordic countries and America

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.760
or the true costs of the policies he champions.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.399
Sanders wants to offer even more generous
benefits than those in Scandinavia

00:13:51.399 --> 00:13:54.699
and thinks that the wealthiest tax payers
can simply foot the bill.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:14:00.260
So you're saying we can pay for all this without
raising taxes on anybody but the 1%?

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:04.260
May have to go a little bit lower than that,
but not much lower.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:07.240
Sanders has proposed a government takeover
of the healthcare sector,

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.000
or about 18% of GDP,

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.280
At a cost of 32 trillion dollars over 10 years.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.940
He wants to increase social security benefits,
offer free public college,

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:19.860
and grant the state sweeping new powers to
tackle climate change through the Green New Deal,

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:23.240
policies that would add at least another 50
trillion to the budget.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.140
When you're dealing with the future of the
planet,

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.660
I don't know how you go too far.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.160
These are not radical, extremist ideas.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.040
I am not coming before the American people
saying 'look,

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.680
I am this radical, wild eyed socialist,

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.199
crazy ideas but listen to me.'

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:42.760
You have more and more growth, producing products
that we do not necessarily need

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:45.320
I mean, you know, at the end of the day you
don't necessarily need

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.800
a choice of 23 underarm spray deodorants

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:53.600
or 18 different pairs of sneakers when children
are hungry in this country.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:58.280
It's all in keeping with his decades long
pattern of ignoring the downsides of centralizing authority

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.700
and massively increasing the size of the government.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:06.819
Massive investments, massive investments,
massive investments, massive investments-

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:12.500
My vision is not just making modest changes
around the edge,

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:15.300
it is transforming American society.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:19.480
So when I use the word socialist, and I know
some people aren't comfortable about it,

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:25.639
I say that it is imperative that we create
a political revolution

00:15:25.639 --> 00:15:27.930
and I hope you will be part of that movement

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:32.870
because if you are, we can in fact transform
this country.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:37.740
So as American voters consider whether to
sign up for part 2 of Sanders' political revolution

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.689
they should consider whether this time, it
really will be different.

00:15:40.689 --> 00:15:43.440
They really were talking about a transformation
of society,

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.839
healthcare in Nicaragua is now free,

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.260
it is terrible, it is very primitive compared
to what we get.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.600
But they now have it free.

